  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the delivery records for all four orders. Two qualify for credit, and I've added **$30.00** in total to your account:\n\n**#6501, Saffron Lane (tonight): $25.00 credit added**\nIt was promised for 6:00 PM and handed to you at 6:52 PM, so 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 or more minutes late, the credit is 20% of the subtotal. On your $128.00 subtotal that comes to $25.60, but the maximum for Plus orders is $25.00, so that's what I added.\n\n**#6502, Pho Real (Thursday): $5.00 credit added**\nIt was promised for 7:15 PM and handed to you at 7:45 PM, so 30 minutes late. Plus orders don't have a delivery fee, so for a delay of 16 to 44 minutes the credit is a flat $5.00.\n\n**#6503, Taqueria Luz (Tuesday): no credit**\nAt 5:50 PM you got a push notification moving the delivery time from 6:30 PM to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. That notice came more than 30 minutes before the original time, so 7:00 PM became the promised time. The order was handed to you at 7:12 PM, only 12 minutes later. Credit starts when an order is more than 15 minutes late, so this one doesn't qualify.\n\n**#6504, Burger Barn (last Friday, Oct 16): no credit, unfortunately**\nThis one was 60 minutes late: promised for 7:00 PM, handed to you at 8:00 PM. However, late deliveries can only be compensated within 7 days of handoff, and that window closed at 8:00 PM on Oct 23, yesterday evening. I'm sorry, but I can't add credit for this order.\n\nYour account credit balance is now **$30.00**, and it will be applied to your future orders. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for checking all four. I'd like to push back on a couple of these, though.\n\nOn #6503, I don't remember getting a notification about a courier shortage, and I'd like to see the notice itself. Even if it did come through, it was still 12 minutes late from the time I was told to expect it, and I was waiting at home the whole evening for it.\n\nOn #6504, why does the window start at the handoff and not when I placed the order? I only found out it was late because I was tracking everything in my note, and I didn't know there was a deadline to ask about it. I'd like it looked at again.\n\nAlso, #6502 was missing the summer rolls. I'd like those compensated to my account credit."
  },
